.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt BUSYBOX-CONSOLE-TOOLS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm busybox-console-tools ,
.Nm clear ,
.Nm reset ,
.Nm resize ,
.Nm setlogcons
.Nd BusyBox console tools
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm clear
.Nm reset
.Nm resize
.Nm setlogcons
.Op Ar N
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the console applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
.Bl -tag -width setlogcons
.It Nm clear
Clear the screen.
The VGA console honors both emitted sequences:
.Ql "ESC [H"
moves the cursor home and
.Ql "ESC [J"
erases from the cursor to the end of the screen.
.It Nm reset
Reset the terminal display and restore terminal signal generation,
line buffering, and echo.
The VGA console honors the display reset
.Pq Ql "ESC c" ,
attribute reset
.Pq Ql "ESC [m" ,
and erase
.Pq Ql "ESC [J" .
It ignores the character set selection
.Ql "ESC (B"
and cursor visibility request
.Ql "ESC [?25h" .
.It Nm resize
Query the terminal size and set its recorded window size.
The VGA console honors the cursor save, move, and restore sequences,
but ignores the scroll region request and does not answer the cursor
position query
.Ql "ESC [6n" .
The applet waits for a reply that the VGA console does not supply;
it does not resize that screen.
.It Nm setlogcons
Request that kernel output go to virtual console
.Ar N ;
the default, 0, requests no fixed virtual console.
Rach2 does not provide the Linux virtual consoles or the
.Dv TIOCLINUX
request this applet requires.
It cannot redirect kernel output.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr console 4
